{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1220711-a-question-of-potency","id":1220711,"title":"A question of Potency...","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-05-20T21:00:27-07:00","id":1220711,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon5.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> A question of Potency...","content":"First Edition question [I know, I know... but it's what we play.]:<br /> When casting a spell with a primary consideration of Potency [like a healing Life Arcanum spell] that is affecting multiple targets... is the total potency applied to each target, or is it divided among the several targets?<br /> <br /> e.g.: My Thyrsus casts the Healing Heart spell targeting himself and one other friend, has taken the -2 die penalty for the extra target, and rolls three successes. Does each person receive three points of healing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13169-drkorpal","name":"DrKorpal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-20T21:13:42-07:00","id":1220714,"title":"","content":"If they've taken a penalty to dice to affect subjects then I'm pretty sure the full Potency applies. I'll admit I could be wrong though, I've basically forgotten pretty much all of the 1e mechanics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-20T22:05:48-07:00","id":1220721,"title":"","content":"I'd be inclined to the spell's effect being applied in full to every target (as long as the caster took the appropriate penalties on the roll).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-20T22:31:58-07:00","id":1220728,"title":"","content":"You don't have to split potency, each target gets full effect. Afaik they only time when you split potency in 1ED is when spell itself calls for it or when using combined spells (not sure about the second one).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2636-menace","name":"Menace","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2636_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"527"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-22T17:31:56-07:00","id":1221320,"title":"","content":"It's one potency for the spell and that spell has its effect on the targets. No splitting required.<br /> <br /> This applies to the OP's question as well as combined spells.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}